https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,"Money is deferred time and energy in abstracted form - the crystallization
     of human potential into transferable form."
https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,"Just as Einstein showed us that matter and energy are interchangeable through E=mc², money serves as the mechanism for converting human energy into a storable, transferable form. When you work, create, or provide value to society, you are quite literally transforming your life force - your time, creativity, and physical or mental effort - into an abstract token of that energy."
https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,"What makes money truly remarkable is its ability to crystallize human potential into transferable form. Your knowledge, skills, creativity, and effort - all aspects of your human potential - can be transformed into a medium that others recognize and value."
https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,This crystallization process serves several crucial functions:
https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,Understanding money as crystallized human energy has profound implications. True wealth creation is not about manipulating numbers but about channeling human energy into forms that benefit society. Every honest dollar represents real human effort and ingenuity.
https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,"If money represents human life energy, then its debasement is not just an economic issue but a moral one. Inflation doesn't just reduce purchasing power - it literally dissipates stored human effort."
https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,"The beauty of this understanding lies in its elegant simplicity. While modern financial systems have become incredibly complex, the core truth remains: money is simply deferred time and energy in abstracted form. This simplicity is not a limitation but rather a source of its power."
https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,"Bitcoin makes the energy-money relationship explicit through its proof-of-work system, requiring literal electrical energy to create new units, forming a direct bridge between physical energy and monetary value."
https://satoshinotebook.com/money-is-energy,p,Understanding money as crystallized energy helps us evaluate any monetary system by asking: How well does it preserve human energy across time? How fairly does it facilitate energy exchange between parties? How resistant is it to the unauthorized dissipation of stored energy?
